<?xml version="1.0" encoding="ISO-8859-1"?>
<wps:ProcessDescriptions xmlns:wps="http://www.opengis.net/wps/1.0.0" xmlns:ows="http://www.opengis.net/ows/1.1" xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance" xsi:schemaLocation="http://www.opengis.net/wps/1.0.0 schemas/wps/1.0.0/wpsDescribeProcess_response.xsd" service="WPS" version="1.0.0" xml:lang="en-US">
	<ProcessDescription wps:processVersion="1" storeSupported="true" statusSupported="false">
		<ows:Identifier>MiraMon:CreaMMM:Param1:1</ows:Identifier>
		<ows:Title>Create a map (option 1)</ows:Title>
		<ows:Abstract>Creates a MiraMon map (MMM format), where the number and order of the layers remain constant, but the layer names change.</ows:Abstract>
		<ows:Metadata xlink:title="Title:Maps and cartographic series automatic creation"/>
		<ows:Metadata xlink:title="Abstract:This program creates MiraMon maps (MMM format) rapidly from the command line. An existing map may be used as a template."/>
		<DataInputs>
			<Input minOccurs="1" maxOccurs="1">
				<ows:Identifier>Opcio</ows:Identifier>
				<ows:Title>Option 1</ows:Title>
				<ows:Abstract>The names of the layers and some of the display parameters are entered in the command line.</ows:Abstract>
				<ows:Metadata xlink:title="Param1"/>
				<ows:Metadata xlink:title="Name:Option"/>
				<LiteralData>
					<ows:DataType ows:reference="http://www.w3.org/TR/xmlschema-2/#integer">integer</ows:DataType>
					<ows:AllowedValues>
						<ows:Value>1</ows:Value>
					</ows:AllowedValues>
					<DefaultValue>1</DefaultValue>
				</LiteralData>
			</Input>
			<Input minOccurs="1" maxOccurs="1">
				<ows:Identifier>PlantillaMMM</ows:Identifier>
				<ows:Title>Template MMM</ows:Title>
				<ows:Abstract>The MiraMon map that will serve as a template for all that is not generated by the program. If a template is not wanted the user can enter NUL (only option 1).</ows:Abstract>
				<ows:Metadata xlink:title="Param3"/>
				<ows:Metadata xlink:title="Name:TemplateMMM"/>
				<ows:Metadata xlink:title="AlternativeLiteralData:string" xlink:href="http://www.w3.org/TR/xmlschema-2/#string"/>
				<ComplexData>
					<Default>
						<Format>
							<MimeType>application/x-mmm</MimeType>
							<Encoding>Binary</Encoding>
						</Format>
					</Default>
					<Supported>
						<Format>
							<MimeType>application/x-mmm</MimeType>
							<Encoding>Binary</Encoding>
						</Format>
					</Supported>
				</ComplexData>
			</Input>
			<Input minOccurs="1" maxOccurs="1000">
				<ows:Identifier>CapaPaletaOColor</ows:Identifier>
				<ows:Title>Layer, palette or color</ows:Title>
				<ows:Abstract>This parameter is repeated as many times as necessary. The first time contains a name of a layer. Depending on the nature of the layer other parameters may follow. For a JPG, there is no extra parameters. For a IMG, next parameter can be a palette or an IMG. In the second case another IMG is expected, forming a RGB combination. If the file contains Points no extra parameter is needed. If the file contains lines/arcs, a palette or a color follows. If the file contains polygons, a palette or a color follows for the border color and another palette or a color follows with the interior. This pattern can be repeated as many times as layers to be included in the map.</ows:Abstract>
				<ows:Metadata xlink:title="Param4"/>
				<ows:Metadata xlink:title="Name:Layers..."/>
				<ows:Metadata xlink:title="AlternativeLiteralData:string" xlink:href="http://www.w3.org/TR/xmlschema-2/#string"/>
				<ComplexData>
					<Default>
						<Format>
							<MimeType>application/x-arc</MimeType>
							<Encoding>Binary</Encoding>
						</Format>
					</Default>
					<Supported>
						<Format>
							<MimeType>application/x-arc</MimeType>
							<Encoding>Binary</Encoding>
						</Format>
						<Format>
							<MimeType>application/x-pnt</MimeType>
							<Encoding>Binary</Encoding>
						</Format>
						<Format>
							<MimeType>application/x-pol</MimeType>
							<Encoding>Binary</Encoding>
						</Format>
						<Format>
							<MimeType>application/x-vec</MimeType>
							<Encoding>ascii</Encoding>
						</Format>
						<Format>
							<MimeType>application/x-img</MimeType>
							<Encoding>Binary</Encoding>
						</Format>
						<Format>
							<MimeType>image/jpeg</MimeType>
							<Encoding>Binary</Encoding>
						</Format>
						<Format>
							<MimeType>application/x-dbf</MimeType>
							<Encoding>Binary</Encoding>
						</Format>
						<Format>
							<MimeType>application/x-p25</MimeType>
							<Encoding>Binary</Encoding>
						</Format>
						<Format>
							<MimeType>application/x-rel</MimeType>
							<Encoding>Binary</Encoding>
						</Format>
					</Supported>
				</ComplexData>
			</Input>
			<Input minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
				<ows:Identifier>TITOL</ows:Identifier>
				<ows:Title>Title</ows:Title>
				<ows:Abstract>The title of the map. If not entered the first layer is used.</ows:Abstract>
				<LiteralData>
					<ows:DataType ows:reference="http://www.w3.org/TR/xmlschema-2/#string">string</ows:DataType>
					<ows:AnyValue/>
				</LiteralData>
			</Input>
			<Input minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
				<ows:Identifier>VERIFICA</ows:Identifier>
				<ows:Title>Verify</ows:Title>
				<ows:Abstract>Indicates that it is necessary to verify the existence of the layer. In option 1, and where a template exists, the program stops. If there is no template the program emits a message but allows the process to continue. For VEC type files, the program always verifies the existence of the file and stops if it doesn't find it because it needs to read the documentation file to identify the file type.</ows:Abstract>
				<LiteralData>
					<ows:DataType ows:reference="http://www.w3.org/TR/xmlschema-2/#string">string</ows:DataType>
					<ows:AllowedValues>
						<ows:Value>##blank##</ows:Value>
					</ows:AllowedValues>
					<DefaultValue>##blank##</DefaultValue>
				</LiteralData>
			</Input>
		</DataInputs>
		<ProcessOutputs>
			<Output>
				<ows:Identifier>NouMMM</ows:Identifier>
				<ows:Title>New MMM</ows:Title>
				<ows:Abstract>Is the MiraMon map to be created.</ows:Abstract>
				<ows:Metadata xlink:title="Param2"/>
				<ows:Metadata xlink:title="Name:NewMMM"/>
				<ComplexOutput>
					<Default>
						<Format>
							<MimeType>application/x-mmm</MimeType>
							<Encoding>Binary</Encoding>
						</Format>
					</Default>
					<Supported>
						<Format>
							<MimeType>application/x-mmm</MimeType>
							<Encoding>Binary</Encoding>
						</Format>
					</Supported>
				</ComplexOutput>
			</Output>
		</ProcessOutputs>
	</ProcessDescription>
	<ProcessDescription wps:processVersion="1" storeSupported="true" statusSupported="false">
		<ows:Identifier>MiraMon:CreaMMM:Param1:2</ows:Identifier>
		<ows:Title>Create series of maps (option 2)</ows:Title>
		<ows:Abstract>Option thought to work map series where the file names are fixed (changing only the directory or the first few letters of the name, for example, to indicate which sheet is which) but for which some layers of some sheets of the series may be missing (for example a small sheet containing no electricity power lines)</ows:Abstract>
		<DataInputs>
			<Input minOccurs="1" maxOccurs="1">
				<ows:Identifier>Opcio</ows:Identifier>
				<ows:Title>Option 2</ows:Title>
				<ows:Abstract>The names of the layers are taken from the template and only the SearchText is changed for the SubstituteText in the layers' paths.</ows:Abstract>
				<ows:Metadata xlink:title="Param1"/>
				<ows:Metadata xlink:title="Name:Option"/>
				<LiteralData>
					<ows:DataType ows:reference="http://www.w3.org/TR/xmlschema-2/#integer">integer</ows:DataType>
					<ows:AllowedValues>
						<ows:Value>2</ows:Value>
					</ows:AllowedValues>
					<DefaultValue>2</DefaultValue>
				</LiteralData>
			</Input>
			<Input minOccurs="1" maxOccurs="1">
				<ows:Identifier>PlantillaMMM</ows:Identifier>
				<ows:Title>Template MMM</ows:Title>
				<ows:Abstract>The MiraMon map that will serve as a template for all that is not generated by the program. If a template is not wanted the user can enter NUL (only option 1).</ows:Abstract>
				<ows:Metadata xlink:title="Param3"/>
				<ows:Metadata xlink:title="Name:TemplateMMM"/>
				<ows:Metadata xlink:title="AlternativeLiteralData:string" xlink:href="http://www.w3.org/TR/xmlschema-2/#string"/>
				<ComplexData>
					<Default>
						<Format>
							<MimeType>application/x-mmm</MimeType>
							<Encoding>Binary</Encoding>
						</Format>
					</Default>
					<Supported>
						<Format>
							<MimeType>application/x-mmm</MimeType>
							<Encoding>Binary</Encoding>
						</Format>
					</Supported>
				</ComplexData>
			</Input>
			<Input minOccurs="1" maxOccurs="1">
				<ows:Identifier>TextABuscar</ows:Identifier>
				<ows:Title>Search text</ows:Title>
				<ows:Abstract>Text to search for within the layer name path in the template map. If no search is desired, specify a string that cannot be found.</ows:Abstract>
				<ows:Metadata xlink:title="Param4"/>
				<ows:Metadata xlink:title="Name:SearchText"/>
				<LiteralData>
					<ows:DataType ows:reference="http://www.w3.org/TR/xmlschema-2/#string">string</ows:DataType>
					<ows:AnyValue/>
				</LiteralData>
			</Input>
			<Input minOccurs="1" maxOccurs="1">
				<ows:Identifier>TextSubstituit</ows:Identifier>
				<ows:Title>Substitute text</ows:Title>
				<ows:Abstract>Replaced text inside layer name path in new map.</ows:Abstract>
				<ows:Metadata xlink:title="Param5"/>
				<ows:Metadata xlink:title="Name:SubstituteText"/>
				<LiteralData>
					<ows:DataType ows:reference="http://www.w3.org/TR/xmlschema-2/#string">string</ows:DataType>
					<ows:AnyValue/>
				</LiteralData>
			</Input>
			<Input minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
				<ows:Identifier>TITOL</ows:Identifier>
				<ows:Title>Title</ows:Title>
				<ows:Abstract>The title of the map. If not entered the first layer is used.</ows:Abstract>
				<LiteralData>
					<ows:DataType ows:reference="http://www.w3.org/TR/xmlschema-2/#string">string</ows:DataType>
					<ows:AnyValue/>
				</LiteralData>
			</Input>
			<Input minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
				<ows:Identifier>VERIFICA</ows:Identifier>
				<ows:Title>Verify</ows:Title>
				<ows:Abstract>Indicates that it is necessary to verify the existence of the layer. In option 1, and where a template exists, the program stops. If there is no template the program emits a message but allows the process to continue. For VEC type files, the program always verifies the existence of the file and stops if it doesn't find it because it needs to read the documentation file to identify the file type.</ows:Abstract>
				<LiteralData>
					<ows:DataType ows:reference="http://www.w3.org/TR/xmlschema-2/#string">string</ows:DataType>
					<ows:AllowedValues>
						<ows:Value>##blank##</ows:Value>
					</ows:AllowedValues>
					<DefaultValue>##blank##</DefaultValue>
				</LiteralData>
			</Input>
		</DataInputs>
		<ProcessOutputs>
			<Output>
				<ows:Identifier>NouMMM</ows:Identifier>
				<ows:Title>New MMM</ows:Title>
				<ows:Abstract>Is the MiraMon map to be created.</ows:Abstract>
				<ows:Metadata xlink:title="Param2"/>
				<ows:Metadata xlink:title="Name:NewMMM"/>
				<ComplexOutput>
					<Default>
						<Format>
							<MimeType>application/x-mmm</MimeType>
							<Encoding>Binary</Encoding>
						</Format>
					</Default>
					<Supported>
						<Format>
							<MimeType>application/x-mmm</MimeType>
							<Encoding>Binary</Encoding>
						</Format>
					</Supported>
				</ComplexOutput>
			</Output>
		</ProcessOutputs>
	</ProcessDescription>
</wps:ProcessDescriptions>